INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(400, 0, 4, 0, 0, 0, 'Blasted Lands', 'The Blasted Lands were once the southern half of the Black Morass, a dark fen of marsh and mire. It was here that Medivh and the warlocks of the Shadow Council opened the Dark Portal, and the orcish Horde poured through into Azeroth. The energies of the gate dried and warped the land into a red and barren waste where lightning flickers without end and even the beasts have grown unnaturally strong. At the close of the Second War the broken Horde made its last stand at the foot of the portal, and afterwards the Kirin Tor raised Nethergarde Keep in the northern hills to keep watch over the gate. The demons never truly left. The dreadlord Razelikh rules the wastes through his Shadowsworn cult and the Dreadmaul ogres, and the Burning Legion''s soldiers gather in the Tainted Scar.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Blasted_Lands (southern part of the Black Morass, dried and warped by the portal''s magic, constant lightning, Nethergarde built by Khadgar and the Kirin Tor, Razelikh and the Shadowsworn, Legion in the Tainted Scar); gameobject 175745 The Dark Portal and the Fall of Stormwind (Medivh and the Shadow Council opened the portal); gameobject 21581 Aftermath of the Second War (last battle at the foot of the portal); npc_text 1351 (beasts changed by the portal''s energy); npc_text 8770 (demons surged from the portal); quest 10119 description (20 years silent)'),
(401, 1, 4, 1, 0, 0, 'Nethergarde Keep', 'Nethergarde Keep stands in the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, a Dalaranian fortress raised after the Second War at the urging of Archmage Khadgar to guard against any new invasion through the Dark Portal. The Kirin Tor have manned it ever since, and its analysts and riftwatchers keep a close eye on the gate. Khadgar himself held command here until the gate was reopened and he led the Alliance into Draenor. Today the keep lives on supplies sent from Darkshire, too many of which go astray on the road, its library holds histories of the portal''s wars, and an ambassador within its walls urges the Alliance to set aside its quarrel with the Horde and face the true enemy.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Nethergarde_Keep (Dalaranian fortress built after the Second War at Khadgar''s behest to prevent further invasions from Draenor, staffed by the Kirin Tor, Khadgar led it until the portal reopened, mage tower); gameobject 21582 Beyond the Dark Portal (portal reopened a few months after Nethergarde''s completion); gameobjects 21581, 21582, 175745 (history books in the keep); DB spawns in area 1438: Nethergarde Analyst 6001, Nethergarde Riftwatcher 6002, Ambassador Ardalan 7826; quests 1395, 1423, 1425 (supplies from Darkshire, lost supplies); quest 2783 description (we fight the wrong enemy); quest 1423 reward text (so many supplies are lost between Darkshire and the keep)'),
(402, 1, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'Garrison Armory', 'In the hills beside Nethergarde Keep, the Garrison Armory is the keep''s working mine. Nethergarde miners, watched over by foremen and engineers, cut mithril and truesilver from the rock, and what they dig is sent to Stormwind in trade for the many supplies a fortress in the wastes cannot produce for itself. Its tunnels run deep beneath the hills. The crews guard their ore jealously, and any Horde prospector who slips inside hoping to work the veins will find the miners turning on him at once.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Garrison_Armory (Alliance mining outpost, miners gather resources for the keep, traded to Stormwind; Horde could mine there but the NPCs attack them); DB spawns: Nethergarde Miner 5996, Foreman 5998, Engineer 5997 in area 1457 and in underground tunnels (negative z) under the hills toward the swamp; Mithril Deposit 150079 and Truesilver Deposit 150081 in area 1457; factiontemplate 1575 (Nethergarde miners hostile to Horde)'),
(403, 1, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Dreadmaul Hold', 'In the northwest corner of the Blasted Lands squats Dreadmaul Hold, once an orc settlement until the Dreadmaul ogres drove the orcs out after the Second War and gave it their own name. Behind its barracks and smithy, ogres, ogre mages and brutes answer to Grol the Destroyer, who serves Razelikh the Defiler. Near his seat stands a stone of binding, where servants the Defiler granted to Grol are held in bondage. Starving snickerfang hyenas lurk at the edges of the camp, and a rarely seen ogre called Mojo the Twisted walks among the brutes.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Hold (northwest corner, ogres forced out the orcs after the Second War and renamed it, barracks and blacksmith, Grol serves Razelikh); quests 2681, 2744 (Servants of Grol, triad granted unending life in the Blasted Lands); DB spawns in area 1437: Dreadmaul Ogre 5974, Ogre Mage 5975, Brute 5976, Grol the Destroyer 7665, Servant of Grol 7669, Stone of Binding 141857, Starving Snickerfang 5984, Mojo the Twisted 8296 (rare)'),
(404, 1, 4, 4, 0, 0, 'Altar of Storms', 'On the western edge of the wastes stands the Altar of Storms, one of the few such altars left in Azeroth, raised here by Lady Sevine, one of the three masters of the Shadowsworn. Her followers keep it: enforcers, warlocks and dreadweavers who have given themselves over to the demon lord Razelikh. Sevine holds court beside the altar, and a stone of binding nearby holds the servants the Defiler granted to her.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Altar_of_Storms_(Blasted_Lands) (western edge, built by Lady Sevine); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn (controlled by the Shadowsworn, one of the remaining altars in Azeroth); DB spawns in area 1441: Shadowsworn Enforcer 6007, Warlock 6008, Dreadweaver 6009, Lady Sevine 7667, Servant of Sevine 7671, Stone of Binding 141859; quest 2681 objectives (Servants of Sevine)'),
(405, 1, 4, 5, 0, 0, 'Rise of the Defiler', 'The craggy peaks at the heart of the Blasted Lands belong to Razelikh the Defiler. His lair sits on the highest summit, reachable only by runes of teleportation, and a spirit called the Deathly Usher, bound eternally to this cursed world, waits below and asks what those who come before him desire. At the summit stands the Altar of the Defiler. Nearby, in a crater, lives Kum''isha the Collector, one of the Lost Ones, who gathers draenethyst in the hope of opening a road back to the world he lost.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Rise_of_the_Defiler (craggy mountains near the middle, home of Razelikh); quest 3628 description (lair atop the highest mountain, teleport runes, use the amulet on the Altar of the Defiler); npc_text 2213 and gossip option ''I wish to face the Defiler.'' (Deathly Usher 8816); DB spawns in area 2517: Deathly Usher 8816, Altar of the Defiler 153205, Kum''isha 7363; creature_text 7363 (why I live in a crater); quest 2521 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector (Lost One)'),
(406, 1, 4, 6, 0, 0, 'The Serpent''s Coil', 'The Serpent''s Coil is a winding cave system in the eastern Blasted Lands, its mouth ringed by the burnt-out shells of orcish buildings left from the Second War. Shadowsworn cultists, thugs and adepts guard it for Archmage Allistarj, the master of this labyrinth and one of the Defiler''s three chief servants. A great fel beast prowls the back cave, and a stone of binding nearby holds the servants the Defiler granted to Allistarj. Redstone basilisks hunt among the ruins.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Serpent%27s_Coil (winding cave system in eastern Blasted Lands, burnt-out orcish structures from the Second War, Allistarj operated his Shadowsworn from within); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde (Kirith roams the back cave of the Serpent''s Coil); quest 2721 description (tortured by Allistarj, screams through the halls of the cave); DB spawns in area 1440: Shadowsworn Cultist 6004, Thug 6005, Adept 6006, Archmage Allistarj 7666, Servant of Allistarj 7670, Stone of Binding 141858, Redstone Basilisk 5990'),
(407, 1, 4, 7, 0, 0, 'Dreadmaul Post', 'Dreadmaul Post is an ogre mound of the Dreadmaul clan, raised in the wastes nearer the Dark Portal, through which the ogres first came from Draenor and close to which they have stayed ever since. Dreadmaul maulers and warlocks hold it, and felbeasts prowl the ground around it. Here too stands a stone of binding where Grol keeps more of the servants the Defiler granted him. Now and then a rarely seen ogre known as Magronos the Unyielding walks among them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Post (ogre mound of the Dreadmaul clan; Dreadmaul remained close to the Dark Portal after coming from Draenor); DB spawns in area 1439: Dreadmaul Mauler 5977, Dreadmaul Warlock 5978, Felbeast 8675, Servant of Grol 7669, Stone of Binding 141857, Magronos the Unyielding 8297 (rare)'),
(408, 1, 4, 8, 0, 0, 'The Dark Portal', 'The Dark Portal looms over the southern Blasted Lands, the colossal gate through which the orcish Horde first came to Azeroth. Shattered at the end of the Second War, it woke once more for a short while, when the Alliance marched through it into Draenor, and then fell silent. Felguard sentries and felhounds roam its approaches, and among them stands a stone of binding where servants of Razelikh are held.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dark_Portal (Horde came through it, destroyed after the Second War, silent about twenty years, Kazzak''s ritual reopened it, Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn with Alliance and Horde pushed the demons back); npc_text 8770 (Relthorn: battle, Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn, camp now calm); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quests 10119, 9407; DB spawns in area 72: Felguard Sentry 6011, Felhound 6010, Servant of Razelikh 7668, Stone of Binding 141812, Relthorn 16841, Dar''toon 19254; gameobject 21582 Beyond the Dark Portal (portal woke again months after Nethergarde was finished, later destroyed from Draenor); quest 10119 description'),
(409, 1, 4, 9, 0, 0, 'The Tainted Scar', 'In the southwest of the Blasted Lands lies the Tainted Scar, where the portal''s energies left the soil the color of blood. It is the Burning Legion''s stronghold on this side of the gate, where felguard elites, manahounds, dreadlords and doomguard commanders gather in strength. After the Legion''s defeat at Mount Hyjal, Lord Kazzak led its remnants here, and from the Scar he sent Razelikh to bring the wastes to heel. At an altar on the northern edge the aged warlock Daio the Decrepit lives among the demons, teaching others to bind them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tainted_Scar (barren soil the color of blood; Kazzak in the Scar until the portal reopened, then entered Outland; Daio settled at its altar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Blasted_Lands (after Hyjal Kazzak led the remaining Legion forces in the Tainted Scar and sent Razelikh to secure the land); DB spawns in area 73: Felguard Elite 8717, Manahound 8718, Doomguard Commander 12396, Dreadlord 8716, Daio the Decrepit 14463; quests 7581-7583'),
(410, 2, 4, 1, 0, 0, 'Razelikh the Defiler', 'Razelikh the Defiler is the dreadlord who rules the Blasted Lands. When the Legion''s host was driven back into the Tainted Scar, Lord Kazzak sent him out to bring the wastes to heel, and the Shadowsworn cult and the Dreadmaul ogres now do his bidding through his three chief servants. His lair crowns the highest summit of the Rise of the Defiler, and he shows himself only when called at the altar there. Then he roars for Ilifar, Keeper of Souls, to face his challengers as his champion, and calls the flames of chaos down upon them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Razelikh_the_Defiler (dreadlord, true name Rakh''likh, Kazzak''s most fearsome lieutenant, tasked with securing the land, united the Shadow Council); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn (formed by uniting Shadow Council sects with the Dreadmaul); creature_text 7664 (Ilifar, your master calls; Let the flames of chaos engulf you; Face my champion, mortals); creature_template 7734 Ilifar <Keeper of Souls>; quest 3628 description (lair atop the highest mountain, Altar of the Defiler); npc_text 1813, 1814 (Loramus Thalipedes, gossip while on quest 3141); quests 2681, 2743, 2744, 3511, 3627, 3628 (descriptions and titles)'),
(411, 2, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'Allistarj, Sevine and Grol', 'Three servants rule the Blasted Lands in Razelikh''s name. Archmage Allistarj is master of the Serpent''s Coil, where Shadowsworn cultists, thugs and adepts guard his labyrinth. Lady Sevine, a warlock of the Shadowsworn, raised the Altar of Storms on the western edge of the wastes, and her enforcers and dreadweavers keep it. Grol the Destroyer, lord of the Dreadmaul ogres, holds Dreadmaul Hold. Beside each of them stands a stone of binding that holds servants the Defiler granted them, and between them they keep the wastes for the dreadlord while he waits on his summit.', 'npc_text 1454 (Allistarj of the Shadowsworn, Sevine warlock of the Shadowsworn, Grol lord of the Dreadmaul); quest 2681 objectives (Servants of Allistarj, Sevine, Grol); quest 2721 description (tortured by Allistarj); quest 2743 description (each underling wears a third of the amulet); quest 2744 description (immortal within the Blasted Lands, nearly unlimited power); npc_text 1815, 1816 (Loramus, gossip while on quest 3141); quest 3627 objectives; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shadowsworn; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Altar_of_Storms_(Blasted_Lands); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreadmaul_Hold'),
(412, 2, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Kirith', 'Kirith the Damned is a great fel beast, a hulking felhound that prowls the back cave of the Serpent''s Coil, deep in the labyrinth Archmage Allistarj holds for the Defiler. It burns away the magic of those who face it and tears through their armor. Yet the beast is not all it seems. When it falls, a ghostly figure rises from the body and lingers for a short while, as if death had set something free: the Spirit of Kirith. To those who have no business with it, the spirit keeps its silence.', 'smart_scripts 7728 (Mana Burn, Pierce Armor; on death casts Spirit of Kirith); creature_template 7728 display 6688 (felhound model); 7729 Spirit of Kirith, npcflag 2 only, no gossip menu or quest greeting; quest 2721 description and reward text; quest 2743 description (Kirith grins, my time here is limited); npc_text 1451, 1452 (Swamp of Sorrows, shown while on quest 2801: captured, tortured in turn with Kirith); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kirith (Horde lieutenant, tortured by Allistarj, soul twisted into a beast, found in the Serpent''s Coil cave; defeating him draws out his spirit); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde (Kirith roams the back cave as a huge felhunter)'),
(413, 2, 4, 4, 0, 0, 'Kum''isha the Collector', 'Kum''isha the Collector is one of the Lost Ones, a draenei exile who lives in a crater near the Rise of the Defiler, stranded far from his homeland. He has given his life to the search for flawless spheres of draenethyst, crystals so rare that draenei have died seeking a single one, for with them he believes he can open a rift back to the world he lost. To his senses every race of Azeroth gives off the same dizzying reek of greed, and since it was greed that cost him his home, he means to let greed carry him back. He pays in trinkets for any fragment brought to him, and despises those who take the payment.', 'npc_text 1302, 1303; quests 2521, 2522, 3501, 3502 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 7363; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kum%27isha_the_Collector (race Lost One; pre-Cataclysm he opens a portal and goes through with other Lost Ones)'),
(414, 2, 4, 5, 0, 0, 'Bloodmages Drazial and Lynnore', 'Bloodmage Drazial and his sister Lynnore, elven practitioners of blood magic, keep a small camp near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands. They believe the energy unleashed when the Dark Portal opened seeped into the beasts of the region and drove them to evolve into their present forms. Drazial studies the body: hyena jowls able to snap through thorium steel, the lungs of blasted boars, the decisive strike of the scorpok. Lynnore studies mind and spirit, from the cunning of the redstone basilisk to the vigor hidden in vulture gizzards. Both distill their findings into potent assays, though Drazial''s love of science never strays far from thoughts of profit.', 'npc_text 1351, 1371; quests 2581-2586 and 2601-2604 (descriptions); quest 2585 description (wealthy beyond our... I mean...); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodmage_Drazial (blood elf, sister Lynnore, stationed near the entrance to the Blasted Lands); DB spawns 7505 and 7506 at -10884,-2935 (map 50,14), faction 35'),
(415, 2, 4, 6, 1, 0, 'Quartermaster Lungertz', 'Quartermaster Lungertz keeps Nethergarde Keep supplied, no easy task at the far end of a road that winds through Deadwind Pass and the Swamp of Sorrows. Crates of powerstones for the keep''s mages must be rushed from Darkshire before their power fades, barrels stamped with his name turn up lost along the way, and whole caravans have gone astray on the swamp road. The keep''s stock of Azoran crystals, a reagent its wizards need, is running low. As he reminds every visitor, Nethergarde always needs more: supplies for its mages'' research and supplies to keep its defenders fit to fight.', 'quest 1395 description and texts; quest 1423 description and reward text; quest 1425 reward text (Azoran Crystals, Biggs'' caravan thought lost); quest_greeting 5393 (Nethergarde always needs more supplies, for the mages'' research and the defenders)'),
(416, 2, 4, 7, 1, 0, 'Watcher Mahar Ba', 'Watcher Mahar Ba is one of the watchers of Nethergarde Keep, a scholar eager to understand the forces at work around him. Some time ago he sent a request to Master Mazen of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences in Stormwind for Khadgar''s Essays on Dimensional Convergence, the writings of the very archmage at whose urging the keep was built, and he still waits for them to arrive.', 'quest 1364 description and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Nethergarde_Keep (built at Khadgar''s behest); DB spawn 5385 in Nethergarde Keep, faction template 53 (hostile to Horde)'),
(417, 2, 4, 8, 1, 0, 'Thadius Grimshade', 'Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf who left Aerie Peak years ago in pursuit of darker knowledge, and now works as a diviner in the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep. His rituals can follow the thread between an object and its owner, though he warns onlookers to make no sound, since a single misstep could spell their doom. He does nothing for free. When the gryphon master of Aerie Peak sought his help to find the lost gryphon Sharpbeak, Grimshade first demanded the medallion of the Zul''Farrak troll Nekrum, hoping to learn how it had lengthened its bearer''s life without paying its unpleasant price.', 'quests 2990, 2991, 2992, 2993 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 8022; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thadius_Grimshade'),
(418, 2, 4, 9, 0, 0, 'Daio the Decrepit', 'Daio the Decrepit is an aged human warlock, once a mage, who has settled at an altar on the northern edge of the Tainted Scar among the Legion''s own soldiers. There he teaches the infernal arts to younger warlocks, above all the binding of greater demons. To cage a doomguard, he teaches, one needs a crystal prison shaped from the Tears of the Hederine, an anti-magic crystal from the demons of Winterspring, bound with the blood of the Wildspawn satyrs of Dire Maul, and even then the demon will fight savagely against capture. He holds no illusions about such power: those who wield it, he says, pay grossly for it.', 'quests 7581, 7582, 7583 (descriptions and reward texts); npc_text 6995; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Daio_the_Decrepit (elderly human warlock, formerly a mage, altar in the northern Tainted Scar, trains recruits, ''we pay grossly for the use of said powers''); broadcast_text 9611 (we pay grossly for the use of said powers)'),
(419, 2, 4, 10, 0, 8, 'Netherwane and Dar''toon', 'At the foot of the Dark Portal two camps stand side by side. Watch Commander Relthorn Netherwane of Nethergarde remembers the battle fought here not long ago, when the keep and the Argent Dawn held back a tide of demons until the kingdoms of Azeroth came to drive them through the gate. He never thought to see the portal open again, and fears the quiet hides the madness beyond it. Warlord Dar''toon of the Horde speaks of the same battle with open envy, wishing he had been there when the demons clashed with Azeroth''s heroes. Both now send every soldier they can spare through the gate to the war in Outland.', 'npc_text 8770 (Relthorn); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quest 10119 description (I never thought to see this day); quest 9407 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Watch_Commander_Relthorn_Netherwane (Nethergarde)'),
(420, 3, 4, 1, 0, 8, 'Through the Dark Portal', 'For twenty years the Dark Portal stood silent, a monument to wars half forgotten. The histories kept at Nethergarde tell its story. Opened by Medivh and the Shadow Council, it carried the Horde into Azeroth, and when the Horde broke at the end of the Second War its last clans fell at the foot of the gate. A few months after the keep was finished the portal woke again, and Khadgar and Turalyon led the Alliance into Draenor, then destroyed the gate from the far side to spare Azeroth. Then the Burning Legion forced it open once more. Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held until the armies of the Alliance and the Horde drove the demons back. Now both sides call for volunteers, for beyond the gate rages a savage war their commanders fear they cannot win alone.', 'quests 10119, 9407 (descriptions and reward texts); gameobjects 21581, 21582, 175745 (Nethergarde books); npc_text 8770; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dark_Portal (Stair of Destiny is the Outland counterpart in Hellfire Peninsula); quest_template 10288, 10120 (follow-ups start at the Outland end, so 10119 and 9407 are the Blasted Lands entry quests)'),
(421, 3, 4, 2, 0, 0, 'The Fall of the Defiler', 'With the souls of Thrall''s Grasp set free, the regiment''s fallen commander turns to the one man still unaccounted for: his lieutenant Kirith. The two were imprisoned together and tortured by Archmage Allistarj, but Kirith''s will faltered, and his screams rang through the halls of the cave as the experiments went on. That was the last the commander saw or heard of him. As one chapter closes another begins, and the commander''s work against the demon lord who destroyed his regiment, Razelikh the Defiler, is not yet over.', 'quests 2721, 2743, 2744, 3141, 3602, 3621, 3625, 3626, 3627, 3628 (descriptions and reward texts); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Razelikh_the_Defiler; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde'),
(422, 3, 4, 3, 0, 0, 'Kum''isha''s Spheres', 'Somewhere in the Blasted Lands, Kum''isha the Collector insists, flawless spheres of draenethyst can still be found, though draenei have spent whole lifetimes searching for one and died with their purpose unfulfilled. Any creature of the wastes might carry one. He asks anyone willing, greedy as he believes them all to be, to bring him such a sphere in exchange for riches beyond their wildest dreams, for with it he hopes a rift may be opened to his homeland. Meanwhile he buys flawed fragments, which may still serve his people in other ways, paying in trinkets and scorn alike. His junk heap shrinks while theirs grows, which on Draenor, he says, counts as a fair trade.', 'quests 2521, 2522, 3501, 3502 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 7363 groups 0-4; npc_text 1302');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(400, 1, 0, 6, 'The Dark Portal itself stands dark and silent. For twenty years no army has passed through it, and it looms over the southern wastes as a monument to wars half forgotten, watched day and night by the riftwatchers and analysts of Nethergarde.', 'quest 10119 description (for 20 years a silent monument); DB spawns: Nethergarde Analyst 6001, Nethergarde Riftwatcher 6002'),
(400, 2, 6, 6, 'A new shadow has fallen over the wastes. Necropolises of the Scourge hang in the red sky above the heart of the Blasted Lands, and around the necrotic shards beneath them skeletal shocktroopers, ghoul berserkers and spectral soldiers spread across the land while the cultists who serve them labor in their shadow.', 'mod-individual-progression si_gameobjects.sql (Necropolis 181223 and 181374, circles 181227 over areas 4, 1437, 1440, 2517); mod-individual-progression si_creatures.sql (Skeletal Shocktrooper, Ghoul Berserker, Spectral Soldier, Cultist Engineer, Necrotic Shard in areas 4, 1437, 1439, 1440, 2517; phased IPPPHASE); mod-individual-progression IndividualProgression.cpp checkIPPhasing (Blasted Lands areas phased from state 6 until state 7)'),
(400, 3, 7, 7, 'Now the Dark Portal has woken. Demons pour through it in an endless tide, felguards, voidwalkers, infernals and dreadknights with their hounds, and at its foot the Argent Dawn fights a desperate battle beside the mages of Nethergarde and champions of the Alliance and the Horde. If the line breaks, the Argent Dawn warns, there will be no end to the demons'' fire.', 'mod-individual-progression zone_blasted_lands.sql (state 7 phase at the Dark Portal: Invading Felguard 19284, Invading Voidwalker 19287, Invading Infernal 19285, Dreadknight 19288, Portal Hound 19311, Argent Protector 19320, Nethergarde Advisor 19566, Lord Marshal Raynor 19385, Melgromm Highmountain 18969, Agent Proudwell 19942); quest 10259 Into the Breach description'),
(400, 4, 8, 255, 'Twenty years of silence ended when the Burning Legion forced demons through the Dark Portal. Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held them at bay until the armies of Azeroth arrived and drove them back through the gate. Now the Alliance and the Horde march through the wastes and on into Outland, where a savage war rages on the far side.', 'npc_text 8770 (Relthorn); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quests 10119, 9407 descriptions'),
(401, 1, 8, 255, 'Since the gate woke again, Nethergarde has turned to face it. The keep''s defenders held the foot of the portal beside the Argent Dawn when demons surged through, and Watch Commander Relthorn Netherwane now keeps a camp there, sending every soldier he can through the gate to aid the Alliance''s troops in the savage war on the far side.', 'npc_text 8770 (We of Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held at bay a wave of demons); DB spawn 16841 Relthorn at the Dark Portal; mod-individual-progression ipp_aware_npcs.sql gives him npc_ipp_tbc (seen from state 8); quest 10119 description (help our troops on the other side of the gate); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Watch_Commander_Relthorn_Netherwane (Nethergarde)'),
(406, 1, 0, 255, 'The Coil hides a darker story. Here Allistarj imprisoned the captured commander of Thrall''s Grasp and his lieutenant Kirith, and the screams of his experiments rang through the halls. Kirith never left. The fel beast in the back cave is what Allistarj made of him, and the servants bound to the stone nearby are souls of the same fallen regiment.', 'quest 2721 description (tortured by Allistarj, screams through the halls of the cave); quest 2721 reward text (Spirit of Kirith); quest 2681 objectives (Servants of Allistarj)'),
(408, 1, 0, 6, 'Twenty years have passed since then, and the gate stands dark, a silent monument to a time long since forgotten. Only the demons on its approaches and the watchers of Nethergarde, who never take their eyes from it, keep it company.', 'quest 10119 description (for 20 years a silent monument, a eulogy to a time long since forgotten); DB spawns: Nethergarde Riftwatcher 6002'),
(408, 2, 7, 7, 'Now the gate has woken. Battle rages without pause at its foot as demons pour through in an endless tide, and the Argent Dawn, with the mages of Nethergarde and champions of the Alliance and the Horde, fights a desperate fight to stem it. The Argent Dawn''s agent calls on every hero to enter the breach and lend aid.', 'mod-individual-progression zone_blasted_lands.sql (state 7 phase in area 72: invading demons, Argent Protectors and Guardians, Nethergarde Advisors, Watcher Theronus, Lord Marshal Raynor, Melgromm Highmountain); mod-individual-progression IndividualProgression.cpp checkIPPhasing (AREA_THE_DARK_PORTAL: IPP_PHASE_II at state 7); quest 10259 Into the Breach description (Agent Proudwell 19942, The Argent Dawn)'),
(408, 3, 8, 255, 'Twenty years of silence ended when the Burning Legion forced demons through the gate. Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn held them at bay until the kingdoms of Azeroth arrived and drove them back to Outland. The camps at its foot are calm now, and Watch Commander Relthorn Netherwane and Warlord Dar''toon send every soldier they can up the steps and through the gate.', 'npc_text 8770 (Relthorn: battle, Nethergarde and the Argent Dawn, camp now calm); npc_text 9969 (Dar''toon); quests 10119, 9407; DB spawns 16841, 19254 in area 72 (npc_ipp_tbc under mod-individual-progression)'),
(409, 1, 0, 7, 'Kazzak himself still holds the Scar. The towering demon lord commands the Legion''s host on this side of the gate, nursing the sting of defeat at the close of the Third War and swearing that the shadow of the Legion will yet fall over this world.', 'mod-individual-progression boss_lord_kazzak.sql (Lord Kazzak 12397 spawned at -12226.8,-2433.57, area 73 by posarea.py; scale 2.2; creature_text 12397 group 0); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tainted_Scar (Kazzak in the Scar until the portal reopened)'),
(409, 2, 8, 255, 'Kazzak''s reach no longer ends at the Scar. Since the Dark Portal opened once more, the Burning Legion in Outland has answered to him as Doom Lord Kazzak, and his lieutenants drive its war against the armies of Azeroth on the far side of the gate. Here the host he gathered still holds the blood-red soil.', 'quests 10123, 10142 descriptions (Doom Lord Kazzak commands the Burning Legion in Outland, his lieutenants command its troops); DB: Doom Lord Kazzak 18728 spawned on map 530; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tainted_Scar (Kazzak entered Outland when the portal reopened); hellfire.json 348326 Doom Lord Kazzak'),
(410, 1, 0, 255, 'The demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes told the rest. In the age of war Razelikh was the most feared of Kazzak''s lieutenants, and in the Blasted Lands he united the scattered sects of the Shadow Council with the brutish Dreadmaul. It was the ruin of Thrall''s Grasp that sealed the bargain. The regiment''s stolen souls became immortal servants for the three leaders, who took near-limitless power in exchange for eternal service, and the amulet he made for them, worn in three pieces, is the only key that calls him down.', 'npc_text 1813, 1814 (Loramus gossip, shown while on quest 3141, offered on turning in 2744); quest 2744 description; quest 2743 description'),
(410, 2, 0, 255, 'One thing more was needed: the name of the beast. It came from Lord Arkkoroc in Azshara. The Defiler''s true name is Rakh''likh, and once the shattered amulet was whole again, the last charge given to his hunters named him by it.', 'quest 3508 reward text (The name of the beast must be found); quest 3511 description (Rakh''likh); quest 3628 title (You Are Rakh''likh, Demon), offered on turning in 3627'),
(410, 3, 0, 255, 'Razelikh fell at last on his summit, called down to his altar, with Ilifar fighting at his side. Even as he died the Defiler promised his slayers an eternity of anguish and torture, and swore that vengeance would be his.', 'creature_text 7664 group 3 (on death); quest 3628 description and reward text'),
(411, 1, 0, 255, 'The servants at their stones had been men of Thrall''s Grasp, whose souls Razelikh tore out and shared among his lieutenants, three to each. It was Allistarj, too, who held the regiment''s captured commander and his lieutenant Kirith in the Serpent''s Coil and tortured them both, until Kirith''s will faltered and his screams rang through the halls of the cave.', 'quest 2721 description; npc_text 1452, 1453, 1454 (Swamp of Sorrows, shown while on 2801); quest 2681 objectives'),
(411, 2, 0, 255, 'Kirith''s spirit told what makes the three so vital to their master. Each wears around the neck a third of an amulet of Razelikh''s making, the very key needed to summon the demon lord, and he cannot be reached until all three have fallen.', 'quest 2743 description; quest 3627 description (to reach the Defiler you must first destroy the triad)'),
(411, 3, 0, 255, 'Killing them is no simple matter. In exchange for their servitude Razelikh granted each near-limitless power within the Blasted Lands, and the amulet pieces, attuned to their owners'' lifeforce, keep them from death by any ordinary means as long as they remain there. Loramus Thalipedes saw the cruelty of the bargain: just as their servants were bound to the land, so were they, and the price of their immortality was imprisonment and eternal servitude under Razelikh.', 'quest 2744 description; npc_text 1815, 1816 (Loramus gossip, shown while on quest 3141, offered on turning in 2744)'),
(412, 1, 0, 255, 'Kirith had been lieutenant of Thrall''s Grasp. When the regiment was overwhelmed he fell into the hands of Archmage Allistarj, and his commander, captured later, was held beside him, the two tortured in turn. Where the commander endured, Kirith''s will faltered, and his screams rang through the halls of the cave as the experiments went on. What came out of them was the beast. Only in death could what remained of him speak, and his spirit was startled to learn who had sent for him: Trebor, his old commander.', 'quest 2721 description and reward text (Trebor? Trebor sent you?); npc_text 1451, 1452; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kirith'),
(412, 2, 0, 255, 'Kirith''s spirit knew its time was limited and did not mince words. Grinning, it told how the Defiler''s servants guard the secret of summoning their master, for the key to calling him down hangs around their own necks.', 'quest 2743 description'),
(416, 1, 0, 255, 'The essays came at last, though not as planned. The young courier carrying them lost his way in the Swamp of Sorrows and dropped them as he fled from plantlike creatures of the marsh, and a determined traveler brought them on. Mahar Ba had feared his request overlooked, Mazen being bogged down with so many strange happenings. To glimpse the insight of one as great as Khadgar excites him beyond words.', 'quest 1364 description and reward text'),
(421, 1, 0, 255, 'Kirith was found in the Serpent''s Coil, twisted by Allistarj''s experiments into a great fel beast, and only in death could what remained of him speak. His spirit was startled to learn who had sent the messenger: Trebor, his old commander, the fallen hero of the Horde.', 'quest 2721 reward text (Trebor? Trebor sent you?); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fallen_Hero_of_the_Horde'),
(421, 2, 0, 255, 'Kirith did not mince words. The Defiler is shielded by a triad of power, Archmage Allistarj, Lady Sevine and Grol the Destroyer, and each wears around the neck a third of an amulet of Razelikh''s making: the very key needed to summon the demon lord. The triad must be destroyed.', 'quest 2743 description'),
(421, 3, 0, 255, 'That would be no simple task. In exchange for their servitude Razelikh granted the three nearly unlimited power within the Blasted Lands, and the amulet pieces, attuned to their lifeforce, keep them from death as long as they remain there. For help the commander sent his champions across the sea to the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes in Azshara.', 'quest 2744 description'),
(421, 4, 0, 255, 'The search for a weapon led to azsharite crystals from the south of Azshara and to Galvan the Ancient of the Mithril Order in Stranglethorn, who forged fel weapons able to weaken the three. Armed at last, the champions slew the triad and joined the amulet once more, and the Defiler, sensing the break in his chain of command, knew they were coming for him.', 'quests 3141, 3602, 3621, 3625, 3626 (descriptions and reward texts); quest 3627 description and reward text'),
(421, 5, 0, 255, 'They bore the amulet to the altar atop the Rise of the Defiler and called the demon lord down. Razelikh fell, and his severed horn was carried back to the commander, who hailed a day to be remembered for all eternity: the demonic overlord of the Blasted Lands had fallen, and the horn would stand as proof that heroes still exist in this war torn world.', 'quest 3628 description and reward text'),
(422, 1, 0, 255, 'When a sphere at last reached him he could hardly believe his eyes. He set it hovering before him, chanted in an unknown tongue and tore open a rift, crying out to his brethren to rise and go home to Outland before it closed. Afterward, he remarked, one could see why he lives in a crater.', 'quest 2521 reward text; creature_text 7363 groups 0-4; smart_scripts 7363 (runs on 2521 finished)'),
(422, 2, 0, 255, 'Yet Kum''isha counts the conjuration a failure. The hope of the draenei, he says, is as fervent as any greed for trinkets, and he remains hopeful that his next attempt will succeed. He sends the greedy back out into the cursed lands to find him another sphere.', 'quest 2522 description');
